-- title:
--   Cycle map Gᵃᵇ→ H₁(GbackslashT): surjectivity and kernel
-- statement:
--   Let a group $G$ act on a type $W$ carrying a simple graph $\mathcal T$ whose adjacency is preserved by the action, and suppose $\mathcal T$ is a tree. Suppose given $\tau : W \to \mathbb{Z}/2$ that is $G$-invariant ($\tau(g\cdot w)=\tau(w)$) and takes distinct values on adjacent vertices, i.e. a $G$-invariant proper $2$-colouring, so the action is without inversions. Write $\mathrm{QuotEdge}$ for the set of $G$-orbits of darts of $\mathcal T$ and $\mathrm{QuotVert}$ for the set of $G$-orbits of vertices. Let $E$ be a finite type, $V$ a type, and $D$ a degeneracy datum on $(E,V)$, consisting of maps $a,b : E\to V$ and weights $E\to\mathbb{Z}_{>0}$; let $eE$ identify $E$ with those dart orbits whose chosen representative has source of colour $0$, and $eV$ identify $V$ with the vertex orbits, compatibly with the degeneracy maps: $eV(a(e))$ is the orbit of the source and $eV(b(e))$ the orbit of the target of the representative dart of $eE(e)$. Fix a base vertex $v_0$, and let $\Phi$ be an additive homomorphism from $\mathrm{Additive}(G^{\mathrm{ab}})$ to the ribbon kernel of $D$ — the submodule of $\mathbb{Z}^E$ annihilated by both pushforwards along $a$ and along $b$ — whose value on the class of $g$ is, as a function $E \to \mathbb{Z}$, the cycle $\mathrm{pathCycle}$ obtained by counting, with dart indices relative to the orbit $eE(e)$, the darts of a chosen path from $v_0$ to $g\cdot v_0$. Then $\Phi$ is surjective, and $\Phi(x)=0$ holds exactly when $x$ lies in the additive subgroup generated by the classes of the elements of the vertex stabilisers $\mathrm{Stab}_G(w)$, $w\in W$.
--
--   This is Bass–Serre theory in degree one for an action without inversions on a tree: the quotient map $G \to \pi_1(G\backslash\mathcal T)$ is onto with kernel generated by the vertex stabilisers, here abelianised and expressed through the cycle group (ribbon kernel) of the oriented quotient graph, with no freeness or finiteness of stabilisers assumed. It feeds the construction of period data and uniformisations for Mumford quotients, where for a free (Schottky) action the kernel is trivial and the cycle map becomes an isomorphism $G^{\mathrm{ab}} \cong H_1(G\backslash\mathcal T,\mathbb Z)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_Mumford_surjective_and_apply_eq_zero_iff_mem_closure_stabilizer_of_apply_eq_pathCycle.lean

